# Netlify cache headers.
#
# ONLY the hashed build output is declared here. Everything else keeps Netlify's default
# (`public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`), which is already right for HTML and is what
# production is serving today — a rule for `/*` in this file would risk overriding the
# `/assets/*` rule below depending on match order, for no gain.
#
# `immutable` is safe here and nowhere else: Vite content-hashes these filenames, so the
# hash IS the version. Verified rather than assumed — editing one lazy route moved
# `CVTips-D2YlFVxU.js` to `CVTips-BpQFoncz.js`, and reverting the edit restored the
# original name exactly. A given URL under /assets/ can never change content.
#
# Today every one of these revalidates on every page load: a round trip per chunk, on a
# connection where the round trip is the expensive part. This is the fix for that.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
